# CI-only fixtures, added 2026-09-15: four tests were red on main purely because validation/* swallowed
# the cases they read -- frozen_bc_refusals and les_wallfunction_refusals (backwardFacingStep2D),
# nonorth_vs_openfoam (shearedChannel), determinism_komega (pitzDailyKOmega). The tests pass locally
# because the directories exist on the dev box; CI gets only what is tracked.
!validation/shearedChannel/
!validation/backwardFacingStep2D/
# ...but not its GENERATED fields. C/Cx/Cy/Cz/V/y are postProcess output (cell centres, volumes, wall
# distance), 3.25 MB of the directory's 3.3 MB `0/`, and both codes compute them from the mesh. The
# inputs the tests read -- U, p, k, epsilon, omega, nut, nuTilda -- are 4 KB each.
validation/backwardFacingStep2D/0/C
validation/backwardFacingStep2D/0/Cx
validation/backwardFacingStep2D/0/Cy
validation/backwardFacingStep2D/0/Cz
validation/backwardFacingStep2D/0/V
validation/backwardFacingStep2D/0/y
# pitzDailyKOmega is 38 MB on disk, 21 time directories of a local run. determinism_gate.sh deletes
# every directory except 0/constant/system immediately after copying, so only those are tracked: 2.6 MB.
!validation/pitzDailyKOmega/
validation/pitzDailyKOmega/*
!validation/pitzDailyKOmega/0/
!validation/pitzDailyKOmega/constant/
!validation/pitzDailyKOmega/system/

# The six fixtures behind the remaining SILENT skips, added 2026-09-15. Every one of the 12 non-manifest
# skips in CI was a missing fixture, not a missing tool -- and a skip is worse than a failure because the
# suite still reads green. Same scoping rule as above: the identity gates take an ITERATION COUNT
# (`duct3d_cf 20`, `cav3d_cf 30`), not a reference time, so only 0/constant/system is tracked and the
# leftover local run output (cav3d_cf 193/202, duct3d_cf 151) stays out.
!validation/piov/
# simple_piov_vs_openfoam compares against OpenFOAM's own converged answer, which lives in a SEPARATE
# fixture: it asks for validation/piov_of/393. 752 KB, and without it the gate skips even with piov present.
!validation/piov_of/
!validation/channel/
!validation/tracerBox/
!validation/cav3d_cf/
validation/cav3d_cf/*
!validation/cav3d_cf/0/
!validation/cav3d_cf/constant/
!validation/cav3d_cf/system/
!validation/duct3d_cf/
validation/duct3d_cf/*
!validation/duct3d_cf/0/
!validation/duct3d_cf/constant/
!validation/duct3d_cf/system/
!validation/rotatingCylinders/
validation/rotatingCylinders/*
!validation/rotatingCylinders/0/
!validation/rotatingCylinders/constant/
!validation/rotatingCylinders/system/

# empty_direction_vs_openfoam's ORACLE IS OPENFOAM'S OWN LOG, not a field: it counts `Solving for Uz`
# lines -- 0 in the 2D case, 147 in the 3D one -- to prove brae skips the empty direction exactly as
# OpenFOAM does. Only log.sf is read. The directories holding them are 9.7 MB and 20 MB of run output;
# tracking just the two logs costs 388 KB.
!validation/t3a_of/
validation/t3a_of/*
!validation/t3a_of/log.sf
!validation/duct3d_of/
validation/duct3d_of/*
!validation/duct3d_of/log.sf
!validation/rhoRX/
!validation/rhoPM/
!validation/energyBox/
!validation/rho_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/rhoE_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/suth_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/lu_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/tp_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/fr_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/sst_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/ke_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/luturb_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/sa_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/io_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/ti_vs_openfoam.sh
!validation/abl_vs_openfoam.sh
